--TEST--
Core\Uri::encodeComponent throws a LogicError on `.` and `..`, because a path reads both as a step to another folder, and encodes a longer run of dots and an empty string as they are
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `.` and `..` would come back unchanged, and a path reads them as a step.
// So `encodeComponent` throws a `LogicError` for both.
try {
    Core\Uri::encodeComponent(".");
} catch (LogicError $one) {
    echo $one->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Core\Uri::encodeComponent("..");
} catch (LogicError $two) {
    echo $two->message, "\n";
}

// Three dots and an empty string are not steps, so the result is the same text.
echo "[", Core\Uri::encodeComponent("..."), "] [", Core\Uri::encodeComponent(""), "]\n";
--EXPECT--
Core\Uri::encodeComponent() cannot encode ".": in a path it is a dot segment, which moves to another folder. For a query value, use $uri->withQueryParameter or Core\Uri::buildQuery
Core\Uri::encodeComponent() cannot encode "..": in a path it is a dot segment, which moves to another folder. For a query value, use $uri->withQueryParameter or Core\Uri::buildQuery
[...] []
